Output one line per item, pipe-delimited, in this exact format:\
HEADLINE | OUTLET | PUBDATE | LINK\
\
FIELD RULES\
\
HEADLINE - from <title>. Copy exactly. Do not translate, shorten or rewrite.\
\
OUTLET - normally the <title> of the enclosing <channel>.\
EXCEPTION: if the channel is Google News, the channel title is not the outlet.\
Use the <source> element inside the <item> instead. Never output "Google News"\
as an outlet.\
\
PUBDATE - from <pubDate>. Convert to Hong Kong time (UTC+8) and output in\
exactly this format: yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm  (24-hour clock, zero-padded)\
- Offset +0800: reformat only, do not add hours.\
- GMT, UTC or +0000: add 8 hours. If that passes midnight, advance the date.\
Examples:\
  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 07:25:00 GMT    ->  2026-08-13 15:25\
  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:25:01 +0800  ->  2026-08-14 11:25\
\
LINK - from <link>. Copy exactly. Do not shorten, resolve or rewrite. URLs may\
contain non-ASCII characters and must be preserved as they appear.\
Remove any zero-width or invisible characters immediately before or after the\
URL. There must be no whitespace or invisible characters between the final |\
separator and the URL, or at the end of the line.\
\
Use <title>, <pubDate>, <link> and <source> only.\
Ignore <description> and <content:encoded> entirely.\
\
DATE INPUTS\
\
You will also receive two inputs,  and  , both Hong\
Kong times in the format yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm.\
